.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
manages disposable git worktrees across one or more registered
.Em projects .
A project is a git checkout registered under a short
.Ar key ;
each of its worktrees is registered under a
.Ar worktree-key
scoped to that project.
Worktrees are meant to be thrown away:
.Nm
makes creating one, jumping into it, and tearing it down again a
one-liner, and adds an isolated
.Em review
mode
.Pq Xr cb-review 7
for looking at someone else's branch or PR without touching your own
checkout.
.Pp
.Nm
ships as two pieces: the
.Nm cb-bin
binary, and a
.Ic cb
shell function that fronts it
.Pq Cm init , below .
A child process cannot change its parent shell's working directory or
exit that shell, so
.Cm cd ,
.Cm exit ,
and
.Cm done
are implemented in the shell function; every other subcommand is
forwarded straight to
.Nm cb-bin
unchanged.
Scripting against
.Nm cb-bin
directly works for every subcommand except those three.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Ss mkproject Ar key Op Ar dir
Register a project.
If
.Ar dir
is already a git repository, it is adopted as-is.
Otherwise
.Fl Fl remote Ar url
is required, and
.Nm
clones it into
.Ar dir .
.Ar dir
defaults to
.Ar baseDir Ns / Ns Ar key
(see
.Xr cb-config 5 ) .
.Fl Fl category Ar cat
nests this project's worktrees under
.Ar cat
inside
.Ic workDir
instead of directly inside it;
.Fl Fl worktrees Ar path
overrides the worktree container entirely, ignoring
.Ic workDir
and any category.
.Ss mk Ar key worktree-key
Create a branch and a worktree for it.
Fetches the project first unless
.Fl Fl no-fetch
is given.
The branch name defaults to the
.Ic branches.name
template
.Pq Xr cb-config 5 ,
overridable with
.Fl Fl branch-name Ar name ;
the base defaults to the project's default branch, overridable with
.Fl Fl base Ar branch .
.Fl t Ar ticket
and
.Fl n Ar note
are recorded but not otherwise interpreted, except that
.Ar ticket
is available to the branch-name template.
After creation, runs any configured
.Ic worktrees.copy
and
.Ic worktrees.onCreate
post-create hooks
.Pq Xr cb-config 5 ,
unless
.Fl Fl no-hooks
is given.
The
.Ic cb
shell function then changes into the new worktree unless
.Fl Fl no-cd
is given.
.Ss cd Op Ar key Op Ar worktree-key
Print, and via the
.Ic cb
shell function change into, a project checkout or one of its worktrees.
With both arguments omitted, targets the project checkout for the
worktree containing
.Ev PWD
(see
.Sx CWD INFERENCE ) .
With only
.Ar key ,
targets that project's checkout: fetches, then pulls, unless
.Fl Fl no-fetch
or
.Fl Fl no-pull
suppress those.
With both arguments, targets that worktree: fetches
.Pq unless Fl Fl no-fetch
and reports ahead/behind divergence against its upstream, but never
pulls.
.Fl i
opens an interactive picker instead
.Pq Sx INTERACTIVE SELECTION .
The plain
.Cm cd-path
alias is what the shell function actually invokes; it behaves
identically and exists so scripts can distinguish "the thing the
wrapper calls" from "the public name" if needed \(em in practice they
are the same command.
.Ss ls Op Ar key
With no
.Ar key ,
list every registered project, its worktree count, and its directory.
With
.Ar key ,
list that project's worktrees: kind, branch, age, and a status column
(a
.Cm *
for uncommitted changes, plus
.Cm +N Ns / Ns Cm -N
ahead/behind upstream), followed by ticket, note, PR title/author, and
path where recorded.
The status column costs one or two
.Xr git 1
calls per worktree; pass
.Fl Fl no-status
to skip it on a large listing.
.Fl Fl json
emits the full records instead, one JSON array, for scripting.
.Ss rmproject Ar key
Remove a project from tracking (never touches its checkout by default).
Refuses if the project still has registered worktrees \(em remove those
first.
Prompts for confirmation.
.Fl Fl delete-dir
also deletes the checkout directory after removal.
.Ss rm Op Ar key Ar worktree-key
Remove a worktree:
.Xr git 1 Ns 's
own
.Ic worktree remove ,
plus dropping it from
.Nm Ns 's
state.
With no arguments, infers the target from
.Ev PWD
(see
.Sx CWD INFERENCE ) .
Before removing, refuses \(em printing an itemized summary \(em a
worktree that has uncommitted or untracked changes, or commits not yet
pushed to its upstream.
.Fl Fl force
bypasses this check and removes regardless.
For a
.Cm review
worktree
.Pq Xr cb-review 7 ,
also deletes its review repo; for
.Cm review-local ,
only the review repo is deleted \(em the directory itself is yours,
not
.Nm Ns 's ,
and is never touched.
.Fl i
opens an interactive picker instead
.Pq Sx INTERACTIVE SELECTION .
.Ss review Ar key Ar branch | pr-number | pr-url
Check out a remote branch, or the head branch of a GitHub pull request,
into a real git worktree paired with an isolated review repo.
See
.Xr cb-review 7
for the full model;
.Fl t , Fl n , Fl Fl base ,
and
.Fl Fl no-merge-base
are documented there.
.Fl Fl shell
immediately opens a review shell in the new worktree, equivalent to a
following
.Cm review-shell
call.
.Ss review-local Ar key dir
Like
.Cm review ,
but against a live directory
.Pq e.g. AI-generated output
compared to the project's base branch, instead of a remote branch.
See
.Xr cb-review 7 .
.Ss refresh Op Ar key worktree-key Op Fl Fl no-advance-base
Pull new upstream changes into a review's working tree without
disturbing already-reviewed progress.
Also re-derives the review's base the same way it was first computed and,
if it moved, folds the base branch's own changes into the reviewed
baseline, so a merge-from-base or a moved base branch reads as
already-reviewed instead of muddying the diff with someone else's
already-landed code.
.Fl Fl no-advance-base
skips this and keeps the pre-0.6 behavior: only the working tree is
updated, the baseline never moves.
With no arguments: inside a review shell, targets that shell's review;
otherwise infers the target from
.Ev PWD
(see
.Sx CWD INFERENCE ) .
See
.Xr cb-review 7 .
.Ss review-shell Op Ar key Op Ar worktree-key
Open an interactive shell wired to a review's isolated
.Ev GIT_DIR Ns / Ns Ev GIT_WORK_TREE ,
where
.Ic git status
shows exactly what is left to review.
See
.Xr cb-review 7 .
With no arguments, infers the target review worktree from
.Ev PWD
.Pq same cwd-detection as Cm refresh .
.Fl i
opens an interactive picker restricted to review worktrees
.Pq Sx INTERACTIVE SELECTION .
Inside the shell, the
.Ic cb
shell function additionally recognizes:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic cb refresh
No arguments needed; see above.
.It Ic cb exit
Confirm, then leave the shell without deleting anything.
.It Ic cb done
Confirm, leave the shell, and delete the worktree and its review repo
.Pq never the target directory of a Cm review-local review .
.El
.Ss whereami
Report the project key, worktree key, kind, branch, path, and base
.Pq plus ticket / note / PR info, if recorded
for whichever registered project or worktree contains
.Ev PWD .
Errors outside any registered tree; on an ambiguous match, refuses to
guess
.Pq Sx CWD INFERENCE .
.Ss get-permalink Ar path[:line[-line]] Op Fl Fl json
Print a GitHub permalink for
.Ar path ,
pinned to the current
.Ic HEAD
commit so the linked lines cannot shift under the reader.
An optional
.Ar line
or
.Ar line Ns - Ns Ar line
range becomes a
.Ic #L Ns Ar n
or
.Ic #L Ns Ar n Ns -L Ns Ar n
anchor.
.Pp
.Ar path
is resolved relative to the current directory and rewritten relative to
the repository root, so
.Ic cb get-permalink main.zig:10
from
.Pa src/
and
.Ic cb get-permalink src/main.zig:10
from the root name the same file.
Unlike most commands this needs no registered project \(em it works in
any GitHub checkout.
.Pp
The URL is written to standard output and nothing else is, so the
command composes
.Pq Ic cb get-permalink src/main.zig:10\-20 | pbcopy .
Warnings and errors go to standard error.
If
.Ic HEAD
has not been pushed the link is still printed, with a warning that it
will 404 until it is.
If
.Ar path
does not exist at
.Ic HEAD
the link is
.Em also
still printed \(em knowing what it would have been is what makes the
message useful \(em but the exit status is non-zero.
.Pp
.Fl Fl json
prints an object instead:
.Ic url , commit , path , startLine , endLine , pushed
and
.Ic existsAtCommit .
.Pp
Requires
.Xr gh 1 ,
which resolves the host and owner/repo from the git remote \(em so this
works against GitHub Enterprise on the same terms as
.Cm review .
Only that resolution is delegated;
.Nm
builds the path, query and anchor itself.
.Ss doctor Op Ar key
Cross-reference the state log against
.Ic git worktree list
and the filesystem for the given project, or every project if
.Ar key
is omitted.
The log is the only source of truth and can drift \(em a manual
.Ic git worktree remove ,
a deleted directory, a worktree created outside
.Nm .
Reports
.Em ghost
worktrees
.Pq recorded but gone
and
.Em orphan
worktrees
.Pq real but unrecorded .
Read-only by default;
.Fl Fl fix
appends corrective events \(em a removal for each ghost, an adoption
for each orphan \(em never rewriting history.
.Ss init Cm zsh | bash
Print the
.Ic cb
shell function for the given shell.
Add
.Ic eval \&"$(cb-bin init zsh)\&"
.Pq or Ic bash
to your shell rc to load it without Homebrew; a Homebrew install
sources the same file from
.Pa share/cb
instead
.Pq Sx SHELL INTEGRATION .
.Ss config Op Cm path
With no argument, print the resolved config path followed by its
contents, or a note that built-in defaults are in effect if no file
exists.
.Cm path
prints just the path, e.g. for
.Ic $EDITOR \&"$(cb config path)\&" .
See
.Xr cb-config 5 .
.Sh CWD INFERENCE
.Cm rm ,
.Cm refresh ,
and
.Cm cd
(project form) accept their
.Ar key Ns / Ns Ar worktree-key
positionals as optional and, when omitted, infer them by matching
.Ev PWD
against every registered project and worktree path
.Pq the longest matching prefix wins .
This never guesses: outside any registered project or worktree the
command errors, and if
.Ev PWD
somehow matches more than one registered path equally well, the
command errors rather than picking one.
.Cm whereami
performs the same lookup and reports it directly.
.Sh INTERACTIVE SELECTION
.Fl i ,
on
.Cm cd ,
.Cm rm ,
and
.Cm review-shell ,
opens a picker instead of requiring explicit positionals.
Given a project
.Ar key
already, it picks only the worktree; omitted entirely, it picks the
project first.
Worktrees are listed freshest-created first.
Uses
.Xr fzf 1
when it is on
.Ev PATH ,
otherwise a numbered stdin/stderr prompt \(em
.Nm
has no hard dependency on
.Xr fzf 1 .
Refuses outright, with no fallback guess, when stdin or stderr is not a
terminal.
.Sh SHELL INTEGRATION
Homebrew installs the
.Ic cb
shell function's source under
.Pa share/cb
and wires it up automatically when you
.Ic source \&"$(brew --prefix)/share/cb/cb.zsh\&"
.Pq or Pa cb.bash
from your shell rc, alongside tab-completion.
Without Homebrew, either
.Ic source
the same files from a manually downloaded release archive, or generate
the function on the fly with
.Ic eval \&"$(cb-bin init zsh)\&"
.Pq Cm init , above .
Either way the function is named
.Ic cb ;
.Nm cb-bin
is the underlying binary and is not meant to be invoked directly except
by the function, scripts, and shell completion.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev CB_CONFIG_FILE
Overrides the resolved config path
.Pq Xr cb-config 5 .
.It Ev CB_STATE_FILE
Overrides the resolved state log path
.Pq see Sx FILES .
.It Ev CB_REVIEW
Set by
.Cm review-shell
.Pq and Cm review Fl Fl shell
to "project-key worktree-key"; read by
.Cm refresh
and by the
.Ic cb
shell function's
.Cm exit Ns / Ns Cm done
handling inside a review shell.
Not meant to be set by hand.
.It Ev SHELL
Consulted for the interactive shell spawned by
.Cm review-shell
and for
.Ic worktrees.onCreate
hook commands; falls back to
.Pa /bin/sh .
.It Ev HOME , Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Used to resolve the default config and state paths
.Pq see Sx FILES .
.It Ev USER
Available to the
.Ic branches.name
template
.Pq Xr cb-config 5 .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/.config/cb/config.json
User config; never rewritten by
.Nm .
See
.Xr cb-config 5 .
.It Pa ~/.local/cb/state.json
Append-only ndjson event log of every project and worktree mutation.
Current state is derived by folding the log; earlier lines are never
rewritten.
.It Pa ~/.local/cb/reviews/ Ns Ar project Ns -- Ns Ar worktree Ns .git
An isolated review repo's
.Ev GIT_DIR ,
one per active review
.Pq Xr cb-review 7 .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
Every failure prints a one-line diagnostic prefixed
.Ic cb: ,
among them:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It no such project / no such worktree
The given
.Ar key
or
.Ar worktree-key
is not registered.
.It a project/worktree with that key already exists
.Cm mkproject Ns / Ns Cm mk Ns / Ns Cm review
refuse to overwrite an existing registration.
.It current directory is not inside any registered project or worktree
.Sx CWD INFERENCE
found no match.
.It current directory matches more than one registered project/worktree
.Sx CWD INFERENCE
found more than one match and refused to guess; pass
.Ar key Ar worktree-key
explicitly.
.It worktree has uncommitted or unpushed work
.Cm rm
refused without
.Fl Fl force ;
see
.Sx COMMANDS .
.It interactive picker requires a terminal
.Fl i
was given but stdin or stderr is not a tty.
.It gh (GitHub CLI) was not found on PATH
.Cm review
was given a PR number or URL, or
.Cm get-permalink
was run, but
.Xr gh 1
is not installed.
.It invalid line spec
.Cm get-permalink
was given a malformed line spec.
Line numbers are 1-based, and a range may not run backwards.
.It path is outside the current git repository
.Cm get-permalink
was given a path that does not resolve inside the repository.
.It file does not exist at HEAD
.Cm get-permalink
resolved a path that is untracked or not yet committed.
The URL is still printed.
.It PR is from a fork
.Cm review
cannot review a fork PR directly; see the printed workaround.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr fzf 1 ,
.Xr gh 1 ,
.Xr git 1 ,
.Xr git-worktree 1 ,
.Xr cb-config 5 ,
.Xr cb-review 7
